use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../buttons/ToggleButton import ToggleButton
from ../TextField import TextField

export ui-component PasswordInput:
    description:
        A password input is a text field for typing a password, hidden as it's
        typed, with a button that shows or hides it. It helps the user check
        what they typed without leaving it on screen.

    composes:
        - @{TextField}
        - @{ToggleButton}

    hiding:
        The password starts hidden, each character shown as a dot or similar,
        unless the component says otherwise. Hidden or shown, the text itself
        is the same.

    revealing:
        The show button is a ToggleButton next to the field. Pressing it shows
        the password as plain text, and pressing it again hides it. Focus goes
        back to the field afterwards, with the caret where it was, so the user
        can keep typing. The component can also show or hide it, and is told
        when the user does.

    name:
        The button has a name such as "Show password", which stays the same
        either way. Whether it is pressed says whether the password is shown.

    resetting:
        The password is hidden again when the form it belongs to is submitted
        or reset, so it isn't left showing.

    passwordManagers:
        The component can say whether this is the user's current password or
        a new one being chosen. This lets the platform and password managers
        offer to fill it in, or to suggest a strong new one. The component can
        also ask password managers to leave the field alone, such as for a
        field where a password must be typed again by hand. How well that
        request is followed is up to the chosen library and the password
        managers themselves.

    common:
        Its label, help text, error message, and disabled and read-only states
        work the same way as a TextField's. A disabled field's show button is
        disabled too.

    nonGoals:
        - No strength meter or list of password rules. The component can show
            those alongside it
        - No second field to confirm the password. That's two PasswordInputs
